# Project: AI-Agent Decoupled System
# OS: Windows | Python 3.13 | Single-user

## HARD CONSTRAINTS (NEVER violate)
- NO Docker, npm, Node.js, Redis, RabbitMQ, Celery
- NO multiprocessing or os.fork
- NO authentication (single-user mode)
- IPC: FastAPI REST + WebSockets ONLY (in-memory state)
- Frontend: Vanilla JS + CDN only (Tailwind, Marked.js, DOMPurify)

## Architecture
- Agent process: port 8001 (REST API + WebSocket + LLM)
- UI process: port 8000 (static files + Agent Supervisor)
- Shared code: shared/ module
- DB: SQLite with aiosqlite, WAL mode, busy_timeout=5000

## Code Style
- Always use type hints
- Always async/await for I/O
- Use structlog for logging, NEVER print()
- Use datetime.now(timezone.utc), NEVER datetime.utcnow()
- Max 50 lines per function
- Import order: stdlib → third-party → local

## Database
- ORM: SQLModel with async sessions
- Use sa_column=Column(ForeignKey(..., ondelete="CASCADE"))
- NEVER use Field(ondelete=...) in SQLModel
- Use .is_(None) instead of == None
- Always await session.commit() after writes
- Always await session.rollback() in exception handlers

## Testing
- Framework: pytest + pytest-asyncio
- Mock HTTP with respx
- Run `pytest tests/ -v` after every change
- Test DB: test_app.db (separate from main app.db)

## Anti-patterns
- ❌ Bare `except:` clauses
- ❌ Global variables for chat state
- ❌ Inserting HTML without DOMPurify.sanitize()
- ❌ Storing secrets in code (use .env)
- ❌ websocket.receive_json() without asyncio.wait_for timeout